---
import '../styles/home.css';
const b = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>IGRIS</title>
  <meta name="description" content="IGRIS hands a coding task to a builder agent and a reviewer agent in Herdr. Your own test command says whether the work is done.">
  <link rel="icon" href={`${b}/favicon.svg`} type="image/svg+xml">
</head>
<body>
  <a class="sr" href="#what">Skip to content</a>
  <header class="top">
    <img src={`${b}/logo.svg`} alt="IGRIS" width="56" height="56">
    <a class="chip" href="https://github.com/JlassiRafet/IGRIS">GitHub</a>
  </header>

  <main id="top">
    <section>
      <h1>Agents build. Your shell decides.</h1>
      <p class="lead">A builder agent writes it, a reviewer checks it, your tests decide.</p>
      <div class="actions"><a class="btn" href="#setup">Get started</a><a href="#how">How a task runs</a></div>
    </section>

    <section id="what">
      <h2><span class="n">01.</span>What IGRIS is</h2>
      <p>A pipeline, not another agent. You ask Hermes in a chat app. A decision layer picks the agent and the model. Herdr runs them in panes. Your tests, not the agents, decide when it is done.</p>
      <p>Nothing runs on a server of ours. There is no server.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="how">
      <h2><span class="n">02.</span>How a task runs</h2>
      <p>The decision layer is a switch: plain rules, Laya on your machine, or Jev hosted. A builder agent works in its own worktree and a reviewer reads the result. Then your check command runs.</p>
      <pre><b>$</b> igris run --task "add a retry to the fetch helper"</pre>
      <p>Exit code 0 means done. Exit code 3 means the task needs you. <a href={`${b}/pipeline/`}>See it run</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="setup">
      <h2><span class="n">03.</span>Set it up</h2>
      <p>Run <code>igris setup</code> for a local page that checks your machine and tells you, in plain words, what is ready and what needs a step. It binds to 127.0.0.1 and stops after 30 minutes without use. Prefer to do it by hand? <a href={`${b}/docs/`}>The docs</a> list every step in order.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="agents">
      <h2><span class="n">04.</span>Pick your agents</h2>
      <p>Claude Code builds and Codex reviews by default. IGRIS knows 24 kinds of agent that Herdr can run, so you can swap either one in <code>igris.toml</code>.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="privacy">
      <h2><span class="n">05.</span>What leaves your machine</h2>
      <p>IGRIS has no telemetry. Only what your own tools send to their providers leaves. With Jev, the task text goes to TypeSafe. With a cloud model behind Hermes, your messages go to that provider.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="status">
      <h2><span class="n">06.</span>Where it stands</h2>
      <p>Detection and the local setup page work today. The pipeline editor and the first full release are next. Version 0.0.0 on crates.io only reserves the name.</p>
    </section>

    <footer><a href={`${b}/docs/`}>Docs</a><a href="https://github.com/JlassiRafet/IGRIS">GitHub</a><span>Apache-2.0</span></footer>
  </main>

  <div class="fade" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <div class="dock" id="dock" data-open="false" hidden>
    <ol class="menu" id="menu" aria-label="Sections"></ol>
    <button class="pill" id="pill" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="menu">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 8h16M4 16h16"/></svg>
      Index
      <svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7 14 5-5 5 5"/></svg>
      <span class="pct" id="pct">0%</span>
    </button>
  </div>

  <script>
    // The Index pill is an enhancement: without scripting the sections above are plain and complete.
    const dock = document.getElementById('dock');
    const pill = document.getElementById('pill');
    const menu = document.getElementById('menu');
    const pct = document.getElementById('pct');
    const secs = [...document.querySelectorAll('main h2')].map((h) => {
      const el = h.closest('section');
      const a = document.createElement('a');
      a.href = '#' + el.id;
      a.textContent = h.textContent.replace(/^(\d+\.)/, '$1 ');
      a.addEventListener('click', () => set(false));
      const li = document.createElement('li');
      li.append(a);
      menu.append(li);
      return { el, a };
    });
    dock.hidden = false;
    function set(open) {
      dock.dataset.open = String(open);
      pill.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(open));
    }
    pill.addEventListener('click', () => set(dock.dataset.open !== 'true'));
    document.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => e.key === 'Escape' && set(false));
    document.addEventListener('click', (e) => !dock.contains(e.target as Node) && set(false));
    function tick() {
      const h = document.documentElement.scrollHeight - document.documentElement.clientHeight;
      const p = h > 0 ? Math.round((100 * scrollY) / h) : 0;
      pct.textContent = Math.min(100, Math.max(0, p)) + '%';
      let cur = null;
      for (const s of secs) if (s.el.getBoundingClientRect().top < innerHeight * 0.4) cur = s;
      for (const s of secs) s.a.setAttribute('aria-current', String(s === cur));
    }
    addEventListener('scroll', tick, { passive: true });
    addEventListener('resize', tick);
    tick();
  </script>
</body>
</html>
